         recommended test: Inspecting the recording of a batched request shows a note/marker that it was sent via a batch, while the recording of a directly sent request carries no such note.
           inputs:  A batching client in RECORD mode where (a) the first batched attempt fails transiently (provider.outcomes=['overloaded_error']) then succeeds on retry, (b) a replay of an existing batched recording by both batch and direct clients, and (c) a batched run mixing an Anthropic stage (batched) with a non-Anthropic stage (direct). Nonzero cost_usd from the fake provider.
           detects: The note is added unconditionally on `batched`, but if the batched call fails over or is retried via a direct path, or if the response is served from the replay path, the recording still claims batch, or a directly sent request in a batched run could be recorded as batched. Also cost is halved on the same condition, so note and pricing could mis-indicate origin.
