Ways the change could fail a criterion (what each rating is measured against):

  min-reusable-prefix-per-model
    [boundary_wrong_side] min-reusable-prefix-per-model/opening-at-minimum-not-marked
      The comparison between the opening's token count and the model's minimum may be strict (>) rather than inclusive (>=). An opening of exactly 512 tokens would then go unmarked for Sonnet 5.5, Opus 5.5 and Haiku 5.5. The diff changes only the minimum lookup, so the comparison in mark_reusable_opening is where this would show.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#3
      src/acceptance/llm.py#2
      pairs: 317 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [scope_too_narrow] min-reusable-prefix-per-model/dotted-sonnet-5-5-matches-sonnet-5
      The lookup uses name.startswith(key) on a hyphenated table. A model id written with a dot, such as claude-sonnet-5.5, does not match the 'sonnet-5-5' key but does match the 'sonnet-5' prefix. The minimum for Sonnet 5.5 would then be 1024 instead of 512, and a 512-token opening would go unmarked. The same naming issue could leave Haiku 5.5 and Opus 5.5 on the fallback default, or let them resolve to the wrong entry.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#3
      src/acceptance/llm.py#2
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 313 skipped once the defect was covered
    [scope_too_narrow] min-reusable-prefix-per-model/provider-prefix-parsing-misses-model-name
