  pair-mapping-cache-hit-on-shared-opening
    [scope_too_narrow] pair-mapping-cache-hit-on-shared-opening/opening-key-differs-from-real-opening
      Calls are grouped by the text of the defects block alone. If the request's reusable opening also contains other per-batch content (the tests block, or a schema built from batch ids), calls with equal keys do not share a byte-identical opening. The designated first call then writes a different prefix from the one the followers read, and the followers miss.
