    [missing_case] pair-mapping-cache-hit-on-shared-opening/opening-minimum-table-misclassifies-model
      The minimum reusable opening size is found by longest-prefix matching on the model name. A model whose name merely begins with a shorter key (for example a later minor version, or a model the table does not name) gets the wrong minimum. When the minimum is too high, the breakpoint is not set and nothing is cached. When it is too low, the marker is ignored by the provider.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#2
