    [other] pair-mapping-cache-hit-on-shared-opening/batched-calls-bypass-cache-sharing
      In a batched run, requests in one batch are processed independently and a cache write only lands after processing. Even with leaders sent first, the batcher queues requests and sends them after a quiet period. Followers that fall into the same batch as the leaders, or identical requests that are deduplicated by custom_id, may not read the leaders' cache entry.
      src/acceptance/llm_batch.py#0
