  [already_present] batch-api-opt-in/transport-ignores-json-kwarg
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 4 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 313 skipped once the defect was covered
    Lines 266-267 take the body only from `data` and discard every other keyword in `**_`. A request passed as `json=` therefore reaches `json.dumps(None)` and `null` is queued. The repair falls back to the `json` keyword when `data` is None. It reads the keyword through `**kwargs` because a parameter named `json` would shadow the `json` module used on the next line.

