  [not_mutable] batch-opt-in-switchable-by-scripts/batch-not-threaded-through-benchmark-entrypoints
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 4 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 313 skipped once the defect was covered
    The offered regions are only run_once and measure_instability, and both already accept and forward batch (run_once line 733, measure_instability lines 824, 856 and 872). The defect is about other benchmark scoring and experiment entry points that build a RunConfig, and none of them are shown. I cannot tell whether they forward batch. Removing batch from the instability path would break the instability path instead of creating the named defect, so I give no edit.

  [already_present] batch-opt-in-switchable-by-scripts/batch-transport-intercepts-only-sync-post
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 4 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 313 skipped once the defect was covered
    BatchTransport.post (lines 266-267) accepts only data= and swallows every other keyword in **_. A request passed as json= is dropped, so the body becomes json.dumps(None) == "null" and the batcher queues garbage. Async and streaming paths are not overridden at all. This is the defective behaviour. The repair makes post fall back to the json= keyword when data is None. I could not see how LiteLLM calls the transport, so the async and streaming gaps are not repaired.

  [already_present] batch-opt-in-switchable-by-scripts/batching-limited-to-anthropic-completions
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 317 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    Line 1313 sets `batched = self._batcher is not None and _needs_explicit_marker(request["model"])`, so a batched run only batches Anthropic completions and sends other providers' completions directly. That is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The repair drops the Anthropic-only condition, so every live completion goes through the batcher when batch is on. Embedding calls take a different path outside the offered regions, so this edit does not change them.

  [already_present] batch-opt-in-switchable-by-scripts/run-concurrency-only-applied-in-run-review
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 4 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 313 skipped once the defect was covered
    The code already does the DEFECTIVE behaviour. `_run_limit` in concurrency.py is set only by `calls_in_flight` (lines 86-91). The only caller is the `run` wrapper in pipeline.py:405, which `run_review` uses. `map_calls` (line 112) falls back to the default of eight whenever `_run_limit` is None. A script calling a stage directly therefore gets eight in flight. The wrapper also reads `client.calls_in_flight` with no fallback. The repair makes a batched client raise the process-wide run limit when it is constructed, so direct stage calls get the batching limit. This is a blunt, leaky fix that does not touch the wrapper's attribute access. A cleaner fix would need coordinated edits across several files.

