  [not_mutable] batched-request-same-recording-key/transport-kwarg-in-request-key
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 4 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 313 skipped once the defect was covered
    The code currently does the EXPECTED behaviour. `_live_call` receives `key` as a parameter, already computed by the caller from `request` (model, messages, schema, controls). The `client` transport is added only to the provider call kwargs (`**transport`, line 1345), and the record stores `request` unchanged. To make the key depend on the transport client, the key derivation would have to change in the caller (`_persist_live_call` or the key function), which is outside the offered regions. Editing only inside `_live_call` cannot change how the key is computed, and putting the client into `request` after the key exists would not make the defect real. So I decline rather than invent an unfaithful edit.

